\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Jesus, Thy wandering sheep behold!
\par See, Lord, with tenderest pity see
\par The sheep that cannot find the fold,
\par Till sought and gathered in by Thee.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Lost are they now, and scattered wide,
\par In pain, and weariness, and want;
\par With no kind shepherd near to guide
\par The sick, and spiritless, and faint.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Thou, only Thou, the kind and good
\par And sheep-redeeming Shepherd art:
\par Collect Thy flock, and give them food,
\par And pastors after Thine own heart.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Give the pure word of general grace,
\par And great shall be the preachers crowd;
\par Preachers, who all the sinful race
\par Point to the all-atoning blood.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Open their mouth, and utterance give;
\par Give them a trumpet-voice, to call
\par On all mankind to turn and live,
\par Through faith in Him who died for all.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. Thy only glory let them seek;
\par O let their hearts with love o'erflow!
\par Let them believe, and therefore speak,
\par And spread Thy mercy's praise below.
\par \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

